   "items": [
    {
     "q": "Who writes the URS, and who answers it?",
     "a": "You write it, and your quality unit approves it. A consultant may draft it for you; the approval stays yours. Suppliers answer it row by row, and the answers often become part of the contract."
    },
    {
     "q": "Will a review from you tie our URS to Aquemi?",
     "a": "No. We propose outcome wording that any capable supplier can answer. Where a row fits only one design, we mark it."
    },
    {
     "q": "Which standards should our URS cite?",
     "a": "Your regulator's good manufacturing practice (GMP) text first, then the USP edition you release to. Name the text, never \"pharma grade\"."
    },
    {
     "q": "We are a small firm. How long should our URS be?",
     "a": "As long as its rows need. A short URS that settles grade, demand, feed water, sanitization and acceptance beats a long copied one. Buying your first system? Start with the plain guide.",
